# ── Python ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# `__pycache__/` has no leading slash: git matches it at ANY depth
# (farm_ontology/*/…, pipelines/, perf/, tests/ — all confirmed in practice).
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/

# ── Secrets & credentials: never commit ───────────────────────────────────
# Values live in Secret Manager (Planet-labs, web-access-token). Runbooks in
# deploy/ write secrets from bytes files, never pipes (CRLF incident).
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*credentials*.json
*service-account*.json
application_default_credentials.json
*planet-api-key*
api-key.txt

# ── Field ops output (device-local, written by the web page + fieldkit) ───
field-notes/

# ── Web app build & deps (reproducible via web/package-lock.json `npm ci`) ─
web/node_modules/
web/.next/
web/out/

# ── Local build / audit / load-test artefacts ─────────────────────────────
# Staged Cloud Build context produced by web/tools/web-image-build.ps1:
.dockerbuild-web/
# Browser audit scratch (Playwright CLI sessions):
.playwright-cli/
# perf/run-load-test.ps1 regenerates these fixed-name files on every run
# (machine output). Deliberately tracked evidence — the dated
# k6-metrics-*.json / after-/baseline- / verdict-k6.json snapshots behind
# perf/RESILIENCE-REPORT*.md — predates these patterns and stays tracked
# (gitignore never applies to files git already tracks).
perf/k6-metrics.json
perf/verdict-*.json
perf/results-stdlib-*.json
perf/load-test-*.log
# k6 binaries resolve under %TEMP%\k6-bin (Find-K6 in perf/run-load-test.ps1),
# OUTSIDE this repo — no pattern needed here.

# ── Packaging / staging tars ──────────────────────────────────────────────
*.tgz

# ── Editors & OS junk ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.idea/
.vscode/
